	(text "Notes:\n- Power enters through the XIAO USB-C only. The XIAO 5V pad (VBUS) feeds the D1 mini 5V pin directly,\n  so don't plug in the AirGradient board's USB-C at the same time.\n- XIAO USB-C faces the same board edge as the D1 mini USB port.\n- J1/J2 follow the D1 mini top-view pinout: pins down to the AirGradient PCB, OLED shield stacks on top.\n- Strapping pins GPIO25 (SDIO edge) and GPIO7 (JTAG source, only with eFuses burnt) only go to the spare D8/D7 pins.\n- D1 mini D0 isn't connected: the XIAO has 11 GPIOs for 12 D1 mini signals.\n- RST goes to the C5's EN through JP1, which is bridged by default. Cut it to disconnect RST.\n- A0 goes straight to GPIO1 (ADC1_CH0) with no divider, unlike the D1 mini's 220k/100k. Keep it under 3.3V.\n- TX/RX use the UART0 IO MUX pins (GPIO11/GPIO12), and D7 uses the SPI2 MOSI IO MUX pin (GPIO7, FSPID).\n- Every other signal is on a GPIO matrix priority 2 pin, except D8, which gets GPIO25 (priority 3, strapping).\n- Net names follow the sensor's pin: S8_TXD/PMS_TXD are ESP inputs, S8_RXD/PMS_RXD are ESP outputs."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 38.1 160.02 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "bbd80607-7329-4aa3-9962-d42ef59bad5d")
	)
